cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the results it produces, please cite it as below."
title: "graf: graph-based surrogate safety analysis"
abstract: >-
  A Python pipeline for computing surrogate safety measures
  (time-to-collision, post-encroachment time, deceleration rate to
  avoid a crash) from video-derived vehicle trajectories, building
  per-frame interaction graphs, and evaluating learned classifiers on
  window-level conflict labels. The repository accompanies a
  pre-registered negative-result study showing that a single scalar
  feature matches or exceeds the trained models on this task.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-04"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Sharqascc/graf"
url: "https://github.com/Sharqascc/graf"
keywords:
  - traffic safety
  - surrogate safety measures
  - time-to-collision
  - graph neural networks
  - reproducibility
  - negative results
